XXI. Citizenship

A federal citizenship could eventually coexist with constituent citizenship.

A person could possess:

Federal Middle Eastern Citizenship

plus

Constituent State Citizenship.

Federal citizenship could guarantee:

* freedom of movement
* federal voting rights
* consular protection
* federal civil rights
* access to federal institutions

Constituent citizenship would preserve local political participation.

